{
  "esm": "1.2.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "process-pm-exhaust-runspec",
    "description": "The `process-pm-exhaust` RunSpec: seven PM running-exhaust pollutant-processes, 728 rows, 104 cohorts on every block. Reproduced from the DEFAULT database: 728 of 728 cells, worst 7.516e-06 -- the same worst cell as the snapshot-path fixture -- and on the port's first run, because the whole computation was reproduced in pandas from the default tables before a line of the model changed.\n\nWHAT IT DISCRIMINATES. (1) `SulfatePMCalculator`, whose chain declaration in `runspecchainedto` is CYCLIC (11801 -> 11501 -> 11801, 11801 -> 11901 -> 11801) and whose arithmetic is not: four species per cohort -- EC, sulfate, water and an internal residue 120 -- and every emitted block a linear combination of them. The split and the re-sum are one share matrix (`spmsh_*`), which is why the cycle never has to be resolved. (2) The fuel-sulfur adjustment of the sulfate fraction, weighted by market share, and the UNADJUSTED residue fraction beside it. (3) BaseRateCalculator's `generalFuelRatio` on a rated pollutant-process -- EC's, `rt_baseFuelRatio` -- and the residue's own copy of it on 12001, which no rate row carries. (4) PM10 chaining off a block that is not rated and not chained but WRITTEN by another calculator. (5) Presence by inner join: electricity's EC and NonECPM are rated at exactly zero and dropped, because `sulfateFractions` has no fuel-type-9 row.\n\nHOW IT GOT HERE, because the first measurement was not only short. On 2026-09-22 the chain emitted 456 rows and 37 were right: EC lacked the base-rate fuel ratio by exactly its value, and the crankcase lift claimed PM sulfate and water through ratio-1 rows that are a row filter inside this calculator -- sulfate came out as ALL of NonECPM (conventions 75). PLAN.md 7.3.24 has the sequence.",
    "authors": [
      "EarthSciML Authors and Contributors"
    ],
    "tags": [
      "runspec",
      "onroad",
      "default-database",
      "process-pm-exhaust",
      "pm",
      "sulfate",
      "share-matrix",
      "cyclic-declaration"
    ]
  },
